{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179991-welcome-to-the-world","id":1179991,"title":"Welcome to the World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-27T17:39:34-08:00","id":1179991,"title":"Welcome to the World","content":"The World of Scion that is. I just finished reading the overview of the World in the first chapter in the provided text on the backerkit, and I thought I would ask what those of us with access to it think of it.<br /> <br /> As for my own thoughts, I think the thing I like most about it, is that its like a nondescript house with all its door and windows opened, where all the rooms are appropriate and essential, but one does not know whether the dining room is on the first or second floor, despite having lived there their whole lives. Nor is it known how many bedrooms there are, or whether there is even a basement.<br /> <br /> There are so many openings and guesses throughout the write up, that just about anyone can mold it in a completely different direction without compromising the integrity of the building, metaphorically speaking of course.<br /> <br /> Is this something that you enjoy or do you prefer things to be set in stone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T06:26:57-08:00","id":1180405,"title":"","content":"Personally I rather like the loose setting elements that allow you to be creative in where you place stuff and how from game to game. Almost all of the specifics are covered because...you know its basically the real world we live in, and there are alot of listed supernal places to play with as well. <br /> <br /> Its a very different scenario than say, Exalted, where not providing any details of the area can really leave you in a lurch given the fantasy world, or at the very least necessitate some serious world building of your own. <br /> <br /> If you need to know whats in Manhattan you can always just google it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}